ack then and it all  pointed toward  parents back then the the major  psychiatrists in our society all were  blaming mom and dad for schizophrenia  and so families like the Galvan's knew  that if they went public with what was  going on that they would be judged and  the family would be destroyed so she had  a lot riding on that yeah you can you  can only imagine Baba Tony to cope well  here before we let you go I wanted to  sneak in a quick question about the  impact that this family and and they're  telling their story has on the wider  scientific understanding of  schizophrenia and how we treat it um  they really have pushed the ball forward  in ways that even surprised them they  were one of the first families to be  studied by the National Institute of  Mental Health back in the 80s when  technology was just starting to give us  a little glimpse into the genome and  they are still the biggest family in the  collection of families with genes like  this and toward the end of Hidden Valley  Road you can learn all about the  different genetic mutations that this  family pointed the way toward that might  help us understand this disease better  and actually might help future  generations it really is an epic story  Robert Colker thank you so much Hidden  Valley Road is on sale now
 

